      "text_raw": "Both islands, the Source and\nthe Drain, have a junction\ncapacitance with respect to\nthe bulk (or substrate). They\ncan easily be added to the\nsmall-signal diagram as\nshown in this slide.\nJunction capacitances\nnormally show a voltage\ndependence described by a\nsquare root, when they are\nreverse biased.\nThe most important one\nis doubtless the Drain-Bulk\ncapacitance C as it\nDB\nappears at the output of the\nMOST amplifier. The\nSource-Bulk capacitance\nC is normally shorted\nSB\nout.",
      "text": "Both islands, the Source and the Drain, have a junction capacitance with respect to the bulk (or substrate). They can easily be added to the small-signal diagram as shown in this slide. Junction capacitances normally show a voltage dependence described by a square root, when they are reverse biased. The most important one is doubtless the Drain-Bulk capacitance C as it DB appears at the output of the MOST amplifier. The Source-Bulk capacitance C is normally shorted SB out."
